---
description: Use when touching auth, API routes, database queries, env vars, payments, or user input
alwaysApply: false
---

- Secrets come from environment variables only. Never hard-code keys, never print them, never commit .env.
- Every API route checks the user is signed in and allowed to touch that record (no trusting IDs from the client).
- Validate all input at the boundary with {{zod}} before using it.
- Use parameterized queries or the ORM; never build SQL with string concatenation.
- {{Supabase}}: never expose the service-role key to the browser; keep row-level security on.
- If a change weakens auth or validation, stop and tell me instead of doing it.
